  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "5 v 5 with gates on the wings",
  "description": "Play 5 v 5 with keepers on a pitch of about 45 × 40 metres. At the halfway line there is a cone gate (about 4 metres) out by each touchline. A team scores both by scoring a goal and by passing the ball through one of the gates to a team-mate on the other side – in either direction. We count a goal as two points and a gate as one, but pick what suits your group.\n\nVariant: 1–2 jokers who play with the team in possession.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Give width – someone should always be available out wide."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Give depth with a run in behind or support behind the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "If the middle is closed – look for the gate on the wing, then keep attacking."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "After a point through the gate: play on towards goal."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
